Article 32-2 (Processing of personally identifiable information) The Minister of Trade, Industry and Resources (including persons entrusted with the authority of the Minister of Trade, Industry and Resources under Article 32), a Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu (including persons delegated or entrusted with the relevant authority if the authority is delegated or entrusted) may process data containing resident registration numbers or alien registration numbers referred to in Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal Information Protection Act if it is essential for conducting the following: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Business affairs to conduct business under Article 5 of the Act;
  2. Business affairs relating to permission to install liquefied petroleum gas storage facilities under Article 8 of the Act;
  3. Business affairs relating to registration, etc. of liquefied petroleum gas transportation businesses under contract under Article 9 of the Act;
  4. Business affairs relating to reporting succession of status of liquefied petroleum gas business operators under Article 12 of the Act;
  5. Business affairs relating to registration of liquefied petroleum gas export or import businesses under Article 17 of the Act;
  6. Business affairs relating to conditional registration of liquefied petroleum gas export and import businesses under Article 18 of the Act;
  7. Business affairs relating to safety education under Article 41 of the Act.
